NIGERIA  BELONGS TO JESUS CHRIST 

The 2nd Commandment:


You shall not misuse the name of the Lord your God!


The name awakens and collects the concept in the person! Whoever desecrates a name and dares to devalue it, thereby devalues ​​the concept! Remember this at all times!


But this clear commandment of the Lord is the one that is least respected of all the Ten Commandments, and is therefore the one that is most violated. There are a thousand different ways of disregarding it. Even if people think that many of its violations are quite harmless, just light expressions, they are still violations of this strictly given commandment!


It is precisely these thousands of supposedly harmless acts of disrespect that degrade the holy name of God and with it the concept of God, which is always closely connected with the name, that rob it of its holiness in the eyes of men, even in the eyes of children, and that sully its inviolability by making it commonplace, by dragging it down into common parlance!


People do not shy away from making themselves look ridiculous. I will not quote one of the many speeches, for the name is far too high and noble for that! But anyone need only pay attention to it for a day and he will be dismayed at the enormous accumulation of violations of the second commandment by people of both sexes, both young and old, right down to children who are barely able to form a proper sentence. For as the old sing, the young twitter!


For this reason, denigration of God is often one of the first things that young people learn in the only seemingly harmless transgressions of God's laws!


The effect of this is the worst of all transgressions! It has spread disastrously among all mankind, not only among Christians, but also among the Mohammedans, Jews and Buddhists; everywhere one hears the same thing ad nauseam!


What value can the name "GOD" have to man then? It is devalued, not even valued as much as the smallest of coins! Much worse, like a worn-out piece of clothing. And this man of the earth, who otherwise wants to be so clever, thinks it is harmless, but sins more than a hundred times a day!


Where is the reflection, where is the slightest stirring of feeling? You too are completely numb to it, just listen to it when the most sacred of all concepts is trampled into the dirt of everyday life!


But make no mistake! The debt account in the afterlife is thus mercilessly burdened for everyone who has sinned in it! And it is not so easy to atone for this, because it has such far-reaching bad consequences, which must take their revenge up to the third and fourth generation, unless there is at least one person in this line of members who comes to the realization of this and puts a stop to this evil behavior.


Therefore, try to fight the harmful habit in the circles you are familiar with. But above all, first cut your own karma threads with all the energy you still have, so that the debt account does not become larger than it already is. Do not believe in an easy release because you have not thought anything bad about it up to now! The damage is therefore exactly the same! And the sin against the commandment remains without fail! You knew it well.


If you did not make a real effort to understand its significance, then that is your fault! Therefore, nothing can be charged against you! Listen and act so that you will be able to redeem many things while you are still on earth.


Otherwise, the quagmire that awaits you when you enter the afterlife and that hinders your upward climb is terrifying.


Yet not only individuals, but also the authorities have shown their resistance to this commandment for centuries by forcibly demanding oaths from people, forcibly urging them to transgress, under threat of earthly punishment if they did not comply. The punishment in the afterlife, however, is much more severe, and it falls on all those who demanded the oath, not on those who had to take it under pressure. Christ also said once again explicitly:


"Let your answer be yes or no; for whatever is more than that is evil."


And the authorities had the power to give the decisive weight to the yes or no by punishing deception in court just as they punished perjury! In this way they were able to raise the value of words in court to the level they needed for a verdict. It was

It is not necessary to force people to break God's commandment!


But the churches and their representatives were even worse, subjecting their fellow human beings to the worst tortures while invoking God, and burning them while invoking God if they had not already succumbed to the torture.


The Roman Emperor Nero, well known to all and notorious for his cruelty, was not as bad in his Christian tortures, not as damnable as many churches with their enormous list of sins against God's laws! Firstly, he did not murder and torture nearly as much, and secondly, he did not invoke God in such hypocritical ways, which must be among the greatest blasphemies a human being can commit.


It is of no use if these same churches condemn today what they unfortunately committed for far too long back then; for they did not give up doing it voluntarily!


And even today, people are not doing much differently, with mutual hostility, just more silent and in a different, more modern form! Here too, only the form has changed over time , not the living core! And this core alone, which people are so keen to hide, counts before God's judgment, never the external form!


And this present form, which only appears harmless, was born of the same unspeakable arrogance of the spirit of the representatives of all the churches as before. And where there is not the damnable arrogance, there is empty conceit, which is based on the earthly power of the churches. These vices often enough result in the most inappropriate enmities, which are then interwoven with earthly calculations for the spread of influence, if not even to the point of a longing for great political significance.


And all this with the name "GOD" on their lips, so that I would like to call out again like the Son of God: "By your actions you have branded my Father's houses, which were supposed to be in your honor, as dens of murder! You call yourselves servants of the word of God, but you have become servants of your own arrogance!"


Every Catholic thinks he is far better in the eyes of God than a Protestant, without there being any reason for it, but every Protestant thinks he is more knowledgeable, more advanced and therefore closer to his God than the Catholic! And these are all those who claim to be followers of Christ, to educate themselves according to his word.


Both parties are fools who rely on something that has no meaning at all in the eyes of God! These people sin far more against the second commandment than followers of other religions, for they misuse God's name not only with words, but with deeds, with their whole way of life, even in their so-called worship.


They give every thinking and careful observer a frightening example of empty forms and empty thinking. It is precisely in the boundless conceit of wanting to make themselves and those around them believe that they already have a place in heaven ahead of those who believe differently that they most deeply desecrate the concept of God!


The external church customs, a baptism and so much else, that is not enough! Only the inner man must face the judgment! Take note of that, you arrogant people, to whom it has already been announced that on the day of judgment they will go about proudly and conceitedly, with flags and splendid garments, in order to joyfully receive their reward. But they will never reach the kingdom of the spirit at the feet of the throne of God, because they will receive the reward that is due to them before they get there. A breath of ice will blow them away like chaff that has no value; for they lack pure humility within themselves and true love for their neighbor!


By their nature they are the worst abusers of the name "GOD", the most severe violators of the second commandment!


They all serve Lucifer, not God! And thereby mock all of God's commandments! From the first to the last! But especially this second one, the violation of which is the blackest smearing of the concept of God in the name!


Be careful not to easily ignore the commandment any more! Now pay close attention to yourself and your surroundings! Remember, if you faithfully fulfill nine commandments and ignore one of them, you will still be lost in the end!


If a commandment is given by God, this is already proof that it is not to be taken lightly, that it must be fulfilled out of absolute necessity! Otherwise it would never have been given to you.


Do not dare to pray unless you are able to resonate with the words with your whole soul, and beware of representing thoughtless chatterers to your God; for you would thereby be guilty of misusing God's name before Him.


Before you ask him for something, think carefully about whether it is urgently needed! Do not get caught up in formal prayers, which have become bad practice at certain times in all religious practices. This is not only an abuse, but blasphemy against the name of God!


In joy or distress, a passionate feeling without words is worth much more than a thousand prayers, even if this feeling only lasts a fraction of a moment. Because such a feeling is always genuine and not hypocritical! Therefore, the term God should never be misused.


It is a holy moment when the human spirit wants to throw itself before the steps of God's throne in supplication or thanksgiving! This must never become habitual chatter! Not even by servants of a church!


The person who manages to use the name God on all possible and impossible occasions has never had the slightest idea of ​​the concept of God! As a human spirit he must have the ability to sense God's presence within himself, even if it is only once in his earthly life! But this one time alone would be enough to take away from him any desire to carelessly violate the second commandment! He will then forever carry within himself the need to only utter the name "GOD" in the utmost purity of his entire inner being!


Anyone who does not have this is far from being worthy of even the word of God, much less of entering God's kingdom and enjoying his blissful presence! For this reason it is also forbidden to create an image of God the Father according to human understanding! Every attempt to do so will only lead to a pitiful reduction, since neither the human mind nor the human hand is capable of seeing even the smallest part of reality in a visionary way and of capturing it in an earthly image! The greatest work of art in this could only mean profound degradation. An eye alone indicates everything in its ineffable radiance.


So sublime is the greatness, incomprehensible to you, which you sum up in the word "GOD" and which you often, in your reckless presumption, dare to use as the most common of empty and thoughtless phrases! You will have to give an account of your actions!


